---
source: crates/odx-cli/tests/cli.rs
expression: cmd.render_long_help().to_string()
---
Migrate addons to another Odoo series, the OCA way: history, pre-commit and odoo-lint fixes

Usage: odx migrate [OPTIONS]
       odx migrate <COMMAND>

Commands:
  addon   Migrate one addon on the branch `<to>-mig-<addon>`: its history from the source series, the repository's pre-commit fixes, then odoo-lint's upgrade fixes as the `[MIG]` commit
  pr      Push the migration branch checked out and open its pull request: to the remote when you may push there, else to your fork (created when missing)
  update  Bring an open migration up to date with what the addon got on the source series since: each new commit replayed with its author, bot commits left out, then odoo-lint's fixes for the target in a `[FW]` commit. On the migration branch checked out, or on someone else's migration pull request
  pin     Pin the dependencies of the migration branch's addon that only exist as an open migration pull request upstream: lines in `test-requirements.txt` pointing at the pull request, in a commit `[DON'T MERGE] test-requirements.txt`, as OCA asks
  unpin   The return trip of a pin: where the pull requests `test-requirements.txt` pins stand, and once every one is merged and released for the target, the `[DON'T MERGE]` commit dropped. `--push` sends the branch to its pull request, `--merge` merges that once its checks are green
  plan    What moving the project to another series takes, addon by addon: available, an open migration pull request to review, or to migrate (dependencies first); own addons apart
  own     Migrate the project's own addons in place: odoo-lint's upgrade fixes and version bump, old migration scripts removed, one `[MIG]` commit per addon; no pull request
  help    Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --continue
          Go on after resolving a conflict in the addon's history

      --abort
          Give up the migration in progress and delete its branch

  -h, --help
          Print help

  -V, --version
          Print version

Global options:
  -C, --project-dir <DIR>
          Run as if started in DIR

  -c, --config <FILE>
          The pyproject.toml to use (a repos.yaml for the commands that read one)

  -j, --jobs <N>
          Override the number of parallel jobs

      --offline
          Serve git repositories and forge and index data from the cache only; what is not cached fails. Local work (git, pre-commit, odoo-lint) takes as long as before

      --fresh
          Ignore cached data; refresh everything before answering

      --no-refresh
          Use cached data even when stale. Like --offline, this saves network time only

      --refresh-index
          Rebuild the addon index for the series involved

      --json
          Machine-readable output on stdout

  -v, --verbose...
          Say when each repository's fetch and build starts, and what each fetched and merged

  -q, --quiet
          Errors only on standard error: no progress lines, no warnings
